---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Vision" description="The Sounio project vision for epistemic computing">
  <section class="section-shell vision-hero relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
      <picture>
        <source
          srcset="/assets/original-artworks/pappou_hero_1280.webp 1280w, /assets/original-artworks/pappou_hero_1536.webp 1536w"
          sizes="100vw"
          type="image/webp"
        />
        <img
          src="/assets/original-artworks/pappou_hero.png"
          alt=""
          class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover object-[right_top] opacity-[0.18] mix-blend-plus-lighter"
          loading="eager"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </picture>
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-[var(--color-bg)] via-[var(--color-bg)]/85 to-[var(--color-bg)]/30"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="container vision-inner relative z-10">
      <span class="badge-pill">Vision</span>
      <h1>Software should express not only what it computes, but what it can justify.</h1>
      <p>
        Scientific pipelines often produce precise numbers without exposing whether those numbers are trustworthy.
        Sounio exists to close that gap inside the language itself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell">
    <div class="container vision-grid">
      <article class="glass glass-specular vision-copy prose">
        <h2>The Problem</h2>
        <p>
          Most languages optimize for throughput and correctness while treating uncertainty as an external concern.
          That disconnect makes reproducibility, auditability, and policy-grade decision making brittle.
        </p>

        <h2>The Direction</h2>
        <p>
          Sounio brings uncertainty, provenance, units, and confidence-gated behavior into first-class language semantics.
          Teams can encode assumptions once and preserve them through every transformation.
        </p>

        <h2>The Commitment</h2>
        <p>
          We build toward systems where scientific claims can be traced from result back to source measurements,
          with explicit confidence boundaries at every step.
        </p>
      </article>

      <aside class="glass vision-seal">
        <img
          src="/assets/emblem/emblem_badge_textperfect_optionC.svg"
          alt="Sounio Language emblem badge"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <p>
          The official emblem is integrated into the V2 trust layer as a durable marker of project identity and execution quality.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .vision-inner {
    max-width: 800px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.95rem;
  }

  .vision-inner h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 5.5vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .vision-inner p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.3vw, 1.16rem);
  }

  .vision-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .vision-copy,
  .vision-seal {
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    padding: 1.15rem;
  }

  .vision-seal {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }

  .vision-seal img {
    width: min(250px, 74vw);
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-radius: 50%;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  }

  .vision-seal p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .vision-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 0.8fr);
    }
  }
</style>
